From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:49:06 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: mock Neo WebGPU adapter discovery natively

Expose a secure-context Chrome 155 WebGPU discovery surface in window and
worker realms: GPU, GPUAdapter, GPUAdapterInfo, GPUSupportedFeatures,
GPUSupportedLimits and WGSLLanguageFeatures. Use native wrappers, real
Promises, stable navigator/subobject identities, readonly setlike behavior,
and descriptor conversion including iterator close and record keys.

Use an Apple A18 Pro persona with normalized apple vendor/architecture,
32-wide subgroups, conservative mocked features/limits and a 16384px
texture dimension consistent with the existing WebGL mock. These are
chosen discovery values, not measurements from a matching Mac.

Match Chrome 155's fallback flag on GPUAdapterInfo; omit removed legacy
GPUAdapter members. Force-fallback and unknown feature-level requests
resolve null; both power preferences select the single integrated GPU.
GPU device execution is intentionally unsupported: requestDevice converts
its descriptor, then rejects with OperationError rather than pretending
to execute GPU commands.

Capture secure-context descriptors and record intrinsics before page code
can replace them; release those handles at context teardown. Keep native
query and rejection objects page-owned and settle promises without a
nested microtask checkpoint.

References:
https://github.com/chromium/chromium/tree/155.0.8059.40/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgpu
https://www.apple.com/macbook-neo/specs/
